Full Access vs Send As

One of the most important lessons from the shared-mailbox practical was that these permissions are different.

Full Access

Allows the user to:

* open the mailbox
* read messages
* manage mailbox contents

Send As

Allows the user to:

* send email appearing directly from the shared mailbox
Therefore: Send As ≠ Full Access.

A user can have:

Send As = Yes

while:

Full Access = No

Victor Kelvin was used to demonstrate this.

Victor had: Send As → Yes
Full Access → No
He could send as IT support, but he could not open/manage the shared mailbox.





